<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee co-op stocks 2.63 mln bags in Jan.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee co-op stocks 2.63 mln bags in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coffee stocks held by Brazilian cooperatives totaled 2.63 million 60.5 kg bags Jan 31, said National Coffee Council (CNC).</p>
<p>That is down from than the 3.21 million bags held by cooperatives as of Dec 31 but up slightly from the 2.39 million bags held at the same stage in 1996.</p>
<p>Sales by cooperatives reached 720,579 bags during January, showing that producers maintained the flow of coffee to market, CNC said.</p>
<p>Cooperatives received 146,822 bags of coffee during the month of January, almost exactly twice the 72,371 bags delivered in January 1996, it added.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
